    <div class="legend">
      <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-sw" style="background:var(--iom)"></span>Isle of Man <span style="font-size:9px;color:var(--text-f);margin-left:2px">(est.)</span></span>
      <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-sw" style="background:var(--jer)"></span>Jersey</span>
      <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-sw" style="background:var(--gue)"></span>Guernsey</span>
      <span class="leg-item"><span class="leg-sw" style="background:var(--uk)"></span>UK</span>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap"><div class="chart-canvas-wrap" style="height:290px"><canvas id="projChart" role="img" aria-label="Projected total dependency ratios to 2040">Projected dependency ratios to 2040.</canvas></div></div>
    <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--text-f);line-height:1.6;margin-top:8px;border-left:2px solid rgba(78,201,168,0.22);padding-left:10px;">
      Jersey: Statistics Jersey Population Projections 2025–2080 (Feb 2026) — official. 
      Guernsey: Annual Population Projection Bulletin (Jun 2024) — official. 
      UK: ONS 2022-based national projections — official. 
      IoM: estimated from Cabinet Office demographic trajectory — no equivalent official publication.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-src">
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">Actual data:</strong>
      IoM Cabinet Office Census 2021 (Tables 2.1–2.3) · IoM Census 1996 Table 3; 2001 Table 6 · Statistics Jersey Census 2021 CSV (opendata.gov.je) · Jersey Census 1996 Table 3; 2001 CSV · Guernsey Historic Population xlsx (gov.gg, OGL) · ONS Census 2011 &amp; 2021 (OGL) · IoM Cabinet Office Table 1.2, Dependency Ratios 1976–2021
      <br>
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">2022–2026 estimates (IoM):</strong>
      Quinary age-band deltas calibrated from 2021 census baseline using Statistics Isle of Man Population Report 2025 and Manx Radio summary (Q1 2025 anchor: 84,975); migration-age patterns and school-roll checks applied per band. Population total anchors: 84,523 per Manx Radio (2024); 84,975 per IoM Population Report 2025.
      <br>
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">2022–2026 estimates (Jersey):</strong>
      65+ ageing trend from Statistics Jersey published population projections document. 2021 census characteristics: statistics.gov.je.
      <br>
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">2022–2026 estimates (Guernsey):</strong>
      Working-age and 85+ trends from published Guernsey population projection reporting. 2021 electronic census: BBC coverage and gov.gg.
      <br>
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">2022–2026 estimates (UK):</strong>
      2021 census median age and age shares from ONS; 2022–2026 path from UK ageing/projection support sources consistent with ONS principal projection.
      <br>
      <strong style="color:var(--text-m)">2031–2041 projections:</strong>
      Cohort-shift model from 2026 estimated baseline; consistent with Statistics Jersey Population Projections 2025–2080, Guernsey Annual Population Projection Bulletin 2024, and ONS 2022-based national projections. Not census data.
      <br>
      <em style="color:var(--text-f)">"IoM quinary age-band estimates were calibrated from the 2021 census baseline using the Statistics Isle of Man 2025 population report, migration-age patterns and school-roll checks; Jersey and Guernsey ageing trends were drawn from published population projection documents; UK estimates use census anchors and official ageing/projection support."</em>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-brand">Coalfinch</div>
  </div>

